alEq` must be derived if the tests pass as claimed.\n\nI'm also examining the `dic_changes_do_not_directly_shift_alkalinity` test in chemistry.rs to verify it's sound. The test uses specific seeds for the tank states and checks that alkalinity hasn't changed after 1 hour, but I need to understand what the `chemistry_state` helper does and whether it would have active nitrification that could affect alkalinity during that same hour.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2239,"cache_read_input_tokens":40334,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2239},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7da8a6c4-3a62-48ee-87c3-4c780f36efcf","uuid":"844c43e1-23cb-475e-b78f-6d94e495b36f"}
