{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HuyARg95JXhe6ZhFWZxXr9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good — `SimError` derives `PartialEq`, so `assert_eq!` works. All the code changes are sound. Here is my review:\n\n# Review: APPROVED\n\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\n- [x] **TS-REV-001** — `apply_action` rejects `WaterChangePercent` with unknown `source_profile_id` immediately via `validate_source_profile()` call at `engine.rs:268-273`, returning `SimError` before the action reaches `push_back`. The step-time `validate_water_changes` in `water_change.rs:18-31` is retained as a defensive fallback, now refactored to delegate to the same `validate_source_profile` helper.\n- [x] **TS-REV-003** — `chemistry.rs` no longer mutates `alkalinity_meq_total`. The `ALKALINITY_FEEDBACK_MEQ_PER_MG_C` constant and the 3 lines that applied it are removed. pH is recomputed from existing alkalinity and updated DIC only. Grep confirms only 3 alkalinity mutation sites remain: water change retention/replacement and nitrification.\n- [x] **TS-REV-004** — `update_daily_filter_clogging` in `nitrogen_cycle.rs:366-398` now decays `cleanliness_index` directly from detritus and bioload pressure (`0.03 * detritus_pressure + 0.004 * bioload_pressure`). The old formula's bug — `(1.0 - cleanliness_index)` zeroing out when clean — is fixed. `CleanFilter` at `engine.rs:178-183` restores proportionally: `current + (1.0 - current) * intensity`.\n- [x] **TS-REV-005** — `apply_water_change` in `water_change.rs:56,74` now applies retention/replacement to `dissolved_oxygen_mg_total`. Replacement DO is derived from `do_sat_mg_l(source.temperature_c)`, reusing the existing saturation interpolation.\n- [x] All existing acceptance tests still pass (per impl notes: verified with `cargo test` against the full workspace).\n- [x] New integration test `water_change_do_mixing` (`water_change_do_mixing.rs`) confirms 50% water change DO mixing within 1% tolerance, with all other DO processes zeroed out for isolation.\n- [x] New integration test `filter_cleanliness_decay` (`filter_cleanliness_decay.rs`) confirms cleanliness < 0.99 after 30 days of moderate feeding, fed < unfed, and clogging > 0.\n- [x] New unit test `apply_action_rejects_bad_source_profile` (`validation.rs:70-89`) confirms `apply_action` returns `Err(SimError::UnknownSourceProfile)` and queue remains empty.\n\n## Notes\n- The `water_change_mass_balance.rs` tests were correctly updated to reflect that unknown/invalid profiles are now rejected at enqueue time rather than step time. Tests that need to exercise the step-time fallback now use `Engine::from_parts` with pre-loaded queued actions.\n- The alkalinity test (`dic_changes_do_not_directly_shift_alkalinity`) is sound because default TAN is 0.0, so nitrification produces zero alkalinity consumption during the test hour.\n- The `ADULT_SHRIMP_BIOMASS_G` / `JUVENILE_SHRIMP_BIOMASS_G` constants are duplicated between `chemistry.rs` and `nitrogen_cycle.rs` — minor tech debt but acceptable for v1.\n\n## Commit Message\nfix: early source-profile validation, remove DIC-alkalinity drift, filter cleanliness decay, DO water-change mixing (TS-REV-001,003,004,005)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1485,"cache_read_input_tokens":49575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1485},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7da8a6c4-3a62-48ee-87c3-4c780f36efcf","uuid":"5c7f4215-93b6-4b64-82ba-527cd12e7d32"}
